        <h3>The rule</h3>
        <ul class="rule-list">
          <li>Every button: <code>transform: translateY(-4px)</code> at rest, <code>-6px</code> on
            hover (spring easing, <code>cubic-bezier(.3,.7,.4,1.5)</code>, 250ms), <code>-2px</code> on
            press (34ms snap) — plus a matching two-layer <code>box-shadow</code> (a solid "edge" layer
            and a soft ground shadow) that shrinks and grows with the travel.</li>
          <li><strong>Fill color is not part of this rule</strong> — each site keeps its own background
            and picks a shadow color roughly 60% as light. <code>.pushable-flat</code> in
            <code>styles.css</code> is the reusable drop-in for new buttons; existing components
            reproduce the same numbers directly in their own stylesheet rather than taking on the
            class.</li>
          <li>No more <code>outset</code>/<code>inset</code> borders for press feedback anywhere.</li>
          <li><strong>A radio/tab pair needs a selection signal beyond press physics.</strong>
            <code>.hero-button.active</code> gets a <code>4px</code> dark-pink underline
            (<code>::after</code>) on top of the shared shape — a standalone decision, not part of
            JES-155, made when the underline-only elevation difference proved too subtle.</li>
        </ul>
